[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  it's a new year 2022 and another 12  months ahead of us of new games and a  scary amount of re-releases vying for  your cash and attention all year round  january is renowned for being the  slowest month in the video game industry  yet there are a handful of games worth  your time like usual i've found a few  free experiences to tide you over and a  dumb question at the end of the video  like always let's do this  first we have tom clancy's rainbow six  extraction extraction is firmly based in  the play style of rainbow six siege the  operators the weapons the same slow  pacing and thought goes into everything  but that's where the similarities end as  extraction is not about slaying other  real world players it's a co-op shooter  going up against ai-controlled aliens  your mission is to infiltrate an enemy  stronghold collect the thing the  macguffin and extract again if you were  playing siege back in 2018 you've  technically already tried extraction the  ltm outbreak was the birth of this idea  and it spawned an entire standalone game  ubisoft know this is going to be a tough  sell so here's a cool little extra when  one player buys the game they can invite  two other players to play for free for  two whole weeks allowing friends to try  a game without limits is a great way to  attract more people it's clear that  cooperation and teamwork are integral  playing this game alone just doesn't  work so start talking to your squad  right away see if it's a game for them  from that point it's your choice how you  going breach and clear or stealth the  entire mission it's also been confirmed  that post launch content is coming thick  and fast and right away there is expert  level content end game content added  each week it changes as you climb up the  pro ranks online rainbow six extraction  released on january 20th on playstation  xbox pc and stadia which is still a  thing in 2022  [Music]  next we have a couple of playstation  exclusives which have now come to pc and  i couldn't be happier as of january 14th  pc players can see what all the fuss is  about with god of war the playstation 4  swan song we fill the boots of dad of  boy as they fulfill his mother's dying  wish the journey is emotional and the  bond is created between the two and you  can also throw an axe and you can summon  it back like a big angry bald thor  speaking of thor kratos is no longer in  the greek pantheon and has now ventured  into the nordic world it's almost four  years since the story was told and it  won't look any better than on pc a good  pc that is unlocked frame rates and true  4k are here and available for people  with more money than sense it's gonna  look beautiful with playstation offering  their games up to the pc audience it  should see more of us getting excited  for the next god of war game ragnarok  coming later in 2022  the other playstation pc release is  uncharted legacy of thieves collection  releasing on january 28th on ps5 and pc  at the same time this includes the  sublime uncharted 4 and the criminally  underrated lost legacy a third person  action adventure with tons of cover  shooting here's a great touch if you own  either of those games on ps4 you'll be  able to upgrade to both of them on ps5  for 10  the pricing is kind of weird so here's  the info on screen if you prefer to read  it yourself just pause the video hang on  what's that people who have the ps plus  version of the game cannot upgrade and  the multiplayer portion has been  stripped from the games too  come on sony the playstation 5 upgrade  will support full 4k at 30 frames per  second and if you have a monitor capable  of seeing it 120 frames per second at  1080p which is smooth as silk so play  nathan drake's final adventure one last  time and see where the story is likely  going in years to come  let's do some free stuff there's quite a  lot to go through first up is a  monumentous occasion the juggernaut of  the battle royal family has finally gone  free to play as of january 12th  playerunknown's battleground is free on  playstation xbox and pc after 70 plus  million copies have been sold it's  finally time to give it away for free if  you've been living under a rock you  should know that pubg is arguably the  game which made battle royale into the  world dominating game it is today  fortnite warzone and apex legends all  call this game daddy but like most  daddies the kids have surpassed them 100  players parachute onto an island and  scavenge for weapons and murderize each  other and to be the sole survivor if  this doesn't look like something for you  i still beg you to try it at least it's  like visiting your grandparents at  christmas they can still teach you a  thing or two pubg goes free to play  everywhere on january 12th  [Music]  gamers on ps5 and xbox series can also  play the matrix awakens experience right  now we can't really call this a game  it's more of a showcase for the future  of epic games unreal engine graphically  though this demo is mind-blowing the  detail and filmic aesthetic is a wow  moment this is probably the closest  you'll ever get to feeling like you're  in a movie there's a car chase and  there's tons of easter eggs to find  after the main mission is over it won't  last you a long time but it will open  your mind to the future of what video  games will look like in years to come oh  fortnight llama oh there are a few more  free things you should know about the  ps5 version of rec room has been  released i have no idea why but it's a  thing so if you like 3d shenanigans with  friends in rec room the ps5 has its own  standalone version which runs way  quicker is quite impressive and if  you're a ps plus subscriber and added  final fantasy 7 remake to your library  last year you should know that you now  have the ps5 version already added to  your library completely for free pretty  good move if you ask me although it did  take a bit longer than it should be sure  to check back on wednesday and we'll go  through the new january ps plus games by  the way until then i think that's the  end of the free stuff you can get this  month i'll see you next month  and finally a small hello to an indie  game which is crazy addictive win  jammers 2. the first game was released  back in 1994  and was very simple throw a disc past  your opponent to score that's that's  really it the subtlety comes via  tactical throws and bending the disc  into new positions expect wind jammers  too to be super cheap and likely on ps  plus or games with gold soon after all  the sprites have been hand drawn and  animated giving windjammers 2 a retro  feel which is quite appealing to an old  fart like me so there we have it not  much this month but 7 new releases to  tide you over in january 2022 any take  your fancy if you're still here let's  let's bond a little i want to know what  is the greatest game you've ever played  i look forward to arguing with you in  the comments i'm adam you're awesome  i'll see you next time  hey  [Music]

